{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2156-02-19 03:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. I’ll be your doctor during this stay. You’re here for epigastric pain, nausea, and vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2156-02-19 03:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, same pain as before. Sharp, right here." 
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2156-02-19 03:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I couldn’t keep anything down. I’ve had this for years, always called pancreatitis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2156-02-19 03:17:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. But your lipase is only slightly elevated—112—and your CT scans in the past haven’t shown pancreatitis. We’re starting to think it might not be that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2156-02-19 03:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But the pain is real. It feels just like the other times."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2156-02-19 03:18:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I believe you. The pain is real. But we need to find the right cause. Your GI doctor suggested a HIDA scan to check your gallbladder function."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2156-02-19 03:19:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had so many tests. What’s different this time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2156-02-19 03:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "This test checks how well your gallbladder empties. If it’s not working right, that could cause your symptoms. If it is working, we look elsewhere."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2156-02-19 03:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I just want to feel better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2156-02-19 03:21:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep you NPO for now—no food by mouth—to rest your stomach. IV fluids and pain meds to help you through."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2156-02-19 03:22:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on IV fluids before. How long will this take?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2156-02-19 03:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll reassess daily. The HIDA scan is scheduled for tomorrow. Once we have results, we can plan next steps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2156-02-20 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your HIDA scan is done. Good news—your gallbladder ejection fraction is normal. So it’s not biliary dyskinesia."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2156-02-20 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So not gallbladder, not pancreatitis. Then what is it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2156-02-20 10:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your GI specialist thinks it might be a motility disorder—your gut isn’t moving food smoothly. And you may have visceral hypersensitivity—meaning your nerves are extra sensitive to normal gut activity."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2156-02-20 10:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So my gut’s moving wrong, and I feel it more? That sounds possible."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2156-02-20 10:04:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. It’s not in your head—it’s a real condition. We’ll refer you to a motility specialist after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2156-02-20 10:05:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. Can I try eating again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2156-02-20 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We’ll start with clear liquids today—water, broth—and see how you do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2156-02-21 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You tolerated the clear liquids well. How’s the pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2156-02-21 09:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still there, but less intense. Nausea’s better too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2156-02-21 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. Let’s advance to a soft diet—applesauce, toast, yogurt. Small portions, frequent meals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2156-02-21 09:33:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I can try that. Any restrictions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2156-02-21 09:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Avoid fatty or spicy foods. We’ll monitor for nausea or pain after meals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2156-02-22 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done well on the soft diet. Any vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2156-02-22 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No vomiting. Ate most of breakfast. Felt okay after."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2156-02-22 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. We’ll move you to a regular diet today. Keep portions small."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2156-02-22 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I was worried I’d be stuck on liquids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2156-02-22 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re making good progress. Pain still managed with oral meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2156-02-22 11:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, the Dilaudid helps. I take it when the pain spikes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2156-02-23 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs are stable. Hemoglobin’s a bit low—11.8—but not new. We’re not concerned."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2156-02-23 10:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had anemia before. Is it related?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2156-02-23 10:17:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not likely. It’s mild and stable. Probably from past issues, not this episode."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2156-02-23 10:18:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’m glad the pain’s not getting worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2156-02-24 09:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been on a regular diet for two days with no vomiting. Pain is occasional and controlled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2156-02-24 09:46:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I even had a sandwich yesterday. Felt good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2156-02-24 09:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great progress. We’re thinking you could go home in a day or two."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2156-02-24 09:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Really? That’s wonderful. What about follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2156-02-24 09:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll see your GI doctor soon. And we’re referring you to a motility specialist to look deeper into the gut movement issue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2156-02-24 09:50:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I like that plan. I want answers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2156-02-25 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set for discharge tomorrow. You’ll go home with Dilaudid and Prochlorperazine for symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2156-02-25 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Same as last time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2156-02-25 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Take Dilaudid only as needed for pain, not with alcohol. And be careful—Prochlorperazine can make you drowsy, especially with pain meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2156-02-25 10:03:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll be careful. I don’t drive anyway."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2156-02-25 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. Keep taking your regular meds—Venlafaxine, Imipramine, Prazosin—for your mood and PTSD. They’re important."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2156-02-25 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t missed them. They help me sleep and stay calm."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2156-02-25 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Stress can worsen gut symptoms. Keeping your mental health stable helps your whole body."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2156-02-25 10:07:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I never thought about that connection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2156-02-25 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s real. The gut and brain talk to each other. That’s why we treat both."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re cleared for discharge. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. A little sore, but I can manage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done really well. Remember: follow up with your GI doctor. The motility clinic will call you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll keep the appointments. Thank you for listening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. Your symptoms are real, and we’re going to keep working to understand them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That means a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will go over your meds and discharge papers. Call if pain worsens or you can’t keep food down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’m ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’ll see how you do, and the motility team will help figure out the next steps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m hopeful. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Get some rest at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And keep using your hearing aids—we’ll face you when we talk so you can lip-read."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks for remembering."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We want to make sure you understand everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Alright, I’ll sign the discharge. Nurse will be in shortly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care of yourself."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll be in touch through your GI doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll wait for the call."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take it easy the first few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And eat small meals. Avoid heavy or greasy foods."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve made great progress. Proud of how you’ve handled this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel hopeful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the best thing to hear. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "You too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "See you soon in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Looking forward to it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Alright, I’ll let the nurse know you’re ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2156-02-26 08:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2156-02-19 02:58:00",
    "admission_end": "2156-02-26 16:10:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of recurrent epigastric pain and vomiting, previously attributed to pancreatitis but now under question, was admitted for symptom management and diagnostic evaluation. Initial workup revealed only a mildly elevated lipase and normal imaging, casting doubt on pancreatitis. A HIDA scan showed normal gallbladder ejection fraction, ruling out biliary dyskinesia. The clinical team, in consultation with her gastroenterologist, concluded her symptoms were likely due to an intestinal motility disorder with visceral hypersensitivity. Her diet was advanced from NPO to clear liquids, then soft, and finally regular diet as symptoms improved. Pain and nausea were controlled with oral medications by discharge. She was discharged home with PRN Dilaudid and Prochlorperazine, continuation of psychiatric medications, and referral to a motility specialist for outpatient follow-up. Her mental health conditions remained stable throughout the admission.",
    "problems": [
      "Abdominal pain, epigastric",
      "Nausea with vomiting",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Posttraumatic stress disorder",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Unspecified hearing loss"
    ]
  }
}
